{
  "id": "2026-09-14-suggestions-initialization",
  "scope": "suggestions",
  "kind": "review",
  "date": "2026-09-14",
  "question": "Should rich-text-editor initialize suggestions through plugin configuration like comments, instead of replaying authored edits?",
  "model": "GPT-6 / Codex; exact model variant unavailable",
  "method": "best-api-review/history-v2",
  "trigger": "The user requested harsh honest Best API Review of the rich-text-editor suggestion setup and proposed configuring SuggestionPlugin like CommentsPlugin. This is assessment, without downstream implementation.",
  "requirements": [
    "Open the same multi-author example with suggestions, linked discussion threads and current user Alice, without replaying user commands during mount.",
    "Load authored content, identities, attribution and decisions through one canonical native document; comments retain their independent application record lifecycle.",
    "Keep generic copied Editor components independent of optional feature plugins.",
    "Keep actual input intent and projection local to each mounted view, with correct initial undo state and stable thread-to-change targets."
  ],
  "evidenceReuse": "Reaffirms the native authored and optional-presentation ownership decisions. Rechecked the current rich-text-editor caller, comments initialization, suggestion facade, native import/persistence and native-versus-Plate React view inputs. Earlier behavior and scale receipts remain historical and do not prove setup quality. No external research or behavior suite was repeated for this bounded source review.",
  "summary": "Pursue deleting mounted-editor fixture replay and actor switching: hydrate the authored document and matching comments directly, and reuse native mounted-view initialization instead of a mode effect.",
  "verdict": "pursue",
  "previous": "2026-09-14-suggestions-content-attributes",
  "relation": "reaffirms",
  "alternatives": [
    "Keep current setup or extract a seed helper: rejects the caller protocol but only moves it; runtime author mutation, path/offset coupling, history suppression, dynamic comment targets and per-mount replay remain.",
    "Put suggestions in SuggestionPlugin.initialState like comment threads: rejects a second canonical suggestion store. Comments are application-owned records; authored content, retained content, identities and decisions are part of one saved document.",
    "Maximum-value cut and existing owner reuse: load a prepared native authored document through initialValue and matching thread records through CommentsPlugin.initialState.initialThreads. Stable change IDs remove post-construction thread attachment. Native createAuthoredReviewDocument can prepare imported fixture data outside the mounted lifecycle, but it performs import work and is not the ordinary document-opening path.",
    "Add plugin-configured mode defaults: a potentially useful behavior input, but a global mutable mode would violate exact-view ownership. A new initialization registry or lifecycle hook must show a current benefit over forwarding the native view contract.",
    "Change the Plate facade: native React EditorRoot already accepts EditorViewOptions.authored, while Plate EditorRoot omits it. Exposing that existing input is the strongest current candidate to remove the useLayoutEffect without another mode store or SuggestionPlugin knowledge in generic Editor skins. Detailed shape, inference and lifecycle adoption remain design work.",
    "Replace authored storage or merge suggestions with comments: no justified current job. It would discard canonical content/history authority and couple an optional application discussion lifecycle to document edits."
  ],
  "proofLimits": "Source-only, bounded initialization/API ownership review. No product changes, browser replay, runtime benchmark or parity certification. Existing save/reload and view inputs were inspected, not rerun. The proposed facade must prove stable identities and linked targets, empty initial local undo history, first-render projection, Strict Mode/remount behavior and two independent views. Scope-wide fingerprints are provenance, not a claim that every suggestion operation was audited.",
